Description: fix the terminal handling and the compiler warnings
 Read the terminal size from curses (getmaxyx) instead of a TIOCGWINSZ
 ioctl on stdin, which fails when stdin is not the terminal, and refuse
 terminals smaller than 2x2 instead of dividing by zero. Call endwin()
 before printing the end text, so that the terminal is restored (echo,
 line mode). main() returns 0.
 .
 Compiler warnings: the "5" sprite of part 2 was declared but the "C"
 sprite was drawn twice, a character was compared with NULL, unused
 variables, and a row that could stay uninitialised.
